        title: 'Rondo — refrain and contrast',
        body: 'A recurring refrain (A) alternates with contrasting episodes: A–B–A–C–A–D–A. The simplicity makes it a favourite for final movements — providing formal clarity after the complexity of earlier movements. The refrain provides pleasure through repetition; the contrasting episodes provide surprise. Mozart\'s Piano Sonata K. 331 finale ("Alla Turca") is a rondo in everything but formal labelling. Beethoven\'s Rondo a capriccio Op. 129 ("Rage Over a Lost Penny") is the most exuberant example in the Classical repertoire.',
