        body: 'Gamelan is a collective of bronze percussion instruments — gongs, metallophones (similar to marimbas), xylophones, drums — tuned to one of two scale systems: slendro (5 roughly equally spaced notes) or pelog (7 notes in unequal intervals). The two systems are not compatible and a gamelan is built for one or the other. The music is built from interlocking patterns (kolotomi) — a framework of repeated gong strokes within which multiple instruments play elaborations of the central melody at different speeds and registers. No single player leads; the music emerges from the collective. Debussy\'s encounter with Gamelan at the 1889 Paris Exposition directly influenced his move away from harmonic argument toward layered texture and sonority. Gamelan ensembles are associated with Balinese Hinduism and Javanese court culture — the instruments themselves are considered sacred.',
        tags: ['Bronze percussion', 'Slendro', 'Pelog', 'Kolotomi', 'Influenced Debussy', 'Sacred instruments']
